=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported symptom — Campus 1 (PC5–PC14, VLANs 10/20/30 on mswitch0) unable
to reach Campus 2 (PC1–PC4/dc_pc5, VLANs 5/6 on sshswitch, 10.5.0.0/24 and
10.6.0.0/24) — is not reproducible. Direct inspection of every element in the
inter-campus path shows the network is fully healthy.

OSPF is converged across all routers (router16, router7, router8, router10,
router11, router17, sshswitch), with all adjacencies in Full state. Every
router holds correct OSPF-learned routes to both 10.5.0.0/24 and 10.6.0.0/24,
reachable via the path router16 → router7 → router8 → router17 → sshswitch →
switch4/VLAN5-6. The return path (172.16.10–30.0/24) is equally present in
sshswitch's table via 55.5.1.1 (router17). No ACLs or iptables rules exist
anywhere in the forwarding path. sshswitch's VLAN bridges (br_v5 at
10.5.0.254/24 and br_v6 at 10.6.0.254/24) are UP and correctly bridging
switch4 access ports to the router17 bond uplink. Five independent ping tests
spanning all three Campus 1 VLANs to both Campus 2 VLANs — including the
reverse direction from pc1 to pc8 and from dc_pc5 to pc14 — completed with
0% packet loss and sub-3 ms RTTs.

Root cause: there is no fault. The helpdesk ticket describes a connectivity
problem that does not exist in the current lab state; this is a false-premise
report.

Corrective action: none required on the network side. The help-desk ticket
should be closed as "no fault found / unable to reproduce"; the end-user should
be asked to re-test from their own machines and verify that local host
configuration (default gateway, DNS) is correct.
=== END ===
